rpc : retry accept() on transient errors instead of ending the server

socket_t::accept() returned nullptr on any accept() failure, and the serve
loop in ggml_backend_rpc_start_server then returned, so one client that
reset before it was accepted (ECONNABORTED), a signal (EINTR) or a moment
without file descriptors (EMFILE / ENFILE) ended the whole rpc-server
process with exit status 0. Retry the first two, back off 100 ms on the
others, and log the error code each time. Any other error still fails as
before, now with its code in the log.

Upstream: not submitted yet.
Tracking: borism/llama.cpp#3, borism/ollama-cluster#51, borism/ollama-cluster#82

